<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-stockholm-chainsaw" category="High Gain" order="70" instrument="guitar" style="Death Metal">
  <description>The Swedish death metal buzzsaw: a gyrator-EQ distortion pedal with every knob near full, into a fairly clean master-volume head, so the pedal does all the work. Huge, ripping lows and highs with a hollow middle. Best in B standard; play tremolo riffs and D-beat chords.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Death Metal</tag><tag>Swedish</tag><tag>Rhythm</tag><tag>Buzzsaw</tag><tag>Gate</tag><tag>Downtuned</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarworld.com/features/how-entombed-and-sunlight-studios-gave-birth-to-death-metal-guitar-tone" title="Guitar World: How Entombed and Sunlight Studios gave birth to death metal guitar tone"/>
    <source url="https://articles.boss.info/hm-2-the-sound-of-swedish-death-metal-and-beyond/" title="BOSS Articles: HM-2, the sound of Swedish death metal and beyond"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Left_Hand_Path_(album)" title="Left Hand Path (Wikipedia)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
